  "page1": {
    "title": "The Amazing Machine Inside You",
    "subtitle": "How your digestion, blood, and breathing all work as one team.",
    "body": "Your body is a busy machine that works all day and night. Three systems work together to keep you alive. First, your digestive system breaks food into tiny pieces. The stomach and intestines pull out the energy your body needs. Next, your circulatory system moves that energy everywhere. The heart pumps blood through long tubes called vessels. Blood carries food and oxygen to every cell. Then your breathing system brings in fresh air. The lungs take oxygen from the air you breathe. They also <mark>push out</mark> the gas your body does not need. These three systems talk to each other all the time. When you run, they all work harder together. Your amazing inside machine never takes a break.",
